== Quotations and indentation ==

<blockquote>
A block quotation. Skins vary in whether this gets a rule, an indent, a background or a different
face, and a page that quotes anything at all will show which was chosen.
</blockquote>

: A single indent, which is what a colon does.
:: A second level.
::: And a third, which is how every discussion page on every wiki is laid out.

== Preformatted and code ==

A line beginning with a space is preformatted:

 This block keeps its  spacing   exactly
 and does not wrap, so it is the other way a page ends up with a horizontal scrollbar.

<pre>
A pre block, which is the same element by a different route.
</pre>

----

The rule above is a horizontal rule, which is the last block element MediaWiki draws and the one
most often left at the browser default.

